{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the favor of the dweller in the bush, etc.</b> The meaning is that HaShem will desire to do him good even at a time when Israel is in distress — and this is the sign of the Shekhinah of the bush." "And its saying <b>may it come upon the head of Joseph and upon the crown of the head, etc.</b> The meaning is that the reason stated corresponds to two good qualities found in him: first, that although he was exiled and went down to Egypt, and many circumstances of wickedness surrounded him, he stood firm in his righteousness — as they of blessed memory said (Rashi on Exodus 1:5) on the verse ״וְיוֹסֵף הָיָה בְמִצְרָיִם״ — ״this is Joseph,״ etc. — and this is what he alluded to by saying ״the head of Joseph.״ And corresponding to the fact that he repaid his brothers good for evil, he said ״the nazirite of his brothers״ — for his brothers set him apart (הִזִּירוּהוּ) from their brotherhood, as they of blessed memory expounded (Rashi on Genesis 37:17) on the verse ״נָסְעוּ מִזֶּה,״ and despite this, ״וַיְכַלְכֵּל יוֹסֵף,״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:11.845037444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}